+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Our services need one standard way to refer to a value inside a JSON document. JSON Pointer (RFC 6901) is that standard, and later features (e.g. JSON Patch, RFC 6902) build on it, so it must be correct and shared.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `resolvePointer(document, pointer)`, exported from `src/index.ts`: returns the value a JSON Pointer refers to, and throws if the pointer is not a valid JSON Pointer or does not resolve to a value of the document.
+- Governing standard: RFC 6901 (§3 syntax, §4 evaluation, §5 JSON string representation). Document values follow RFC 8259.
+- Not breaking: this is a new export; the library has no source yet.
+- Out of scope: URI fragment identifier representation (RFC 6901 §6), setting/modifying values, JSON Patch, pointer construction/escaping helpers.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `json-pointer`: parsing and evaluating RFC 6901 JSON Pointers against a JSON document.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- New `src/index.ts` (plus an implementation module under `src/`) and tests under `test/`.
+- Public API gains `resolvePointer`. No runtime dependencies; `package.json` unchanged.
